<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43277" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sĕcūrĭcŭla</span></b> ,
		ae, f.
		dim.
		securis. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A little axe</i>, <i>a hatchet</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 4, 4, 114 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 14, 35</span></i>
			<i>in lemm.</i> (but <i><span class="en">Plin. 18,
				19, 49, § 177</span></i>,
			sericulam).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in carpentry, <i>a
				mortise in the shape of a hatchethead</i>, <i>a
				dovetail</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 4, 7, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 17</span></i> (10, 11,
		8).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
